--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ null pointer constant selected: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Fixed: the satisfaction check now type-checks call atoms in a
manifestly-constant-evaluated context ([temp.constr.atomic]/1 +
[expr.const]), gives the eagerly-converted callee its member template
map ([temp.inst]/1) on top of the class map, folds any non-structural
atom form under the SFINAE guard, and recognizes c_bool constants.
The unviable constrained constructor is removed and pr(const T2&)
converts the literal 0 as a null pointer constant ([conv.ptr]/1).
Header-free.
